> fn1(x: real, y: real) = (x + y) ^ 2
> gn1(x: real, y: real) = x ^ 2 + 2 * x * y + y ^ 2 + 1
> equiv fn1 gn1
fn1 and gn1 differ at 1002001 points of the sample, e.g. x=-10, y=-10: 400 vs 401
> fn2(x: real) = (x ^ 3 - 1) / (x - 1)
> gn2(x: real) = x * x + x + 2
> equiv fn2 gn2
fn2 and gn2 differ at 1000 points of the sample, e.g. x=-10: 91 vs 92
> expand (x + y) ^ 2 - (x ^ 2 + 2 * x * y + y ^ 2 + 1)
  ucas: expand (x + y) ^ 2 - (x ^ 2 + 2 * x * y + y ^ 2 + 1)
expand (x + y)^2 - (x^2 + 2x*y + y^2 + 1)
  = -1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> expand (x ^ 3 - 1) / (x - 1) - (x * x + x + 2)
  ucas: expand (x ^ 3 - 1) / (x - 1) - (x * x + x + 2)
expand (x^3 - 1)/(x - 1) - (x*x + x + 2)
  = -1
  holds where x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
